Z||000000||1FieroGTRacingInc||01-12-2001||10:42 PM||||As before my fuel canister is pouring fuel out after 15 minutes of idle(V~6), out of the bottom part...   This is a replacement canister (new)...  <BR>There is fuel in the line (big one), that goes back to the throttle body..  Is there suppost to be fuel in there??? <BR>Could the small snap on component (i don't know how to desribe it , really) the one that has the spring under it...  hhmmm..  <P>Is there just to much fuel pressure ....  does that have anything to do with the canister???<BR>I dont know fuel just pour's out of the bottom of the canister, even after I shut it off it pour's out for 10 minutes!!!   I Really don't want to be a Fiero Fire Stat...   <BR>            Thank's   Steve<P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||01-13-2001||10:25 AM||||Something is hooked up wrong. The fuel vent line is not pressurized. No liquid fuel should be in it. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FieroGTRacingInc||01-13-2001||12:10 PM||||Thank,s theorge.... That's what I thought!  What or which is hooked up wrong, any idea? I know that it is hard to say with out see it.<P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||6
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||01-13-2001||12:18 PM||||On the V-6 engine, there is no fuel supply at the throttle body, ever. (regulates air intake only)<BR>Check your return line and make sure that it is not blocked (at the fuel rail). It is the line that is farthest away from the pully side of the engine. REMOVE the FUEL CAP! and blow some compressed air through it to clear. From which line is the fuel coming from at the canister?<BR>Sounds like the fuel tank is under pressure somehow.<p>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 01-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FieroGTRacingInc||01-13-2001||01:33 PM||||Indiana.....  There is some fuel(not much,not full)in the biggest of the two lines that wrap around the rear end of the engine. I'm fixing to go outside now and check the return line at the fuel rail...<BR>What would cause my fuel tank to be under pressure??<BR>               Thank's for the help...  Steve<P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Greg Piet||01-13-2001||01:53 PM||||under pressure fuel tank seems to me that the gas cap is not venting... If my memory is operating properly (It does get buggy quite a bit) the gas cap is meant to allow some venting to prevent vapor lock.  if the cap doesnt vent then pressure can build up.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||01-13-2001||01:54 PM||||This is just a thought, But did you try running it with the gas cap off? Maybe if the gas cap vent is clogged/bad the canaster may be sucking up fuel. Has any work been done down by the gas tank? If it was maybe one of the lines down there is hooked wrong.||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FieroGTRacingInc||01-13-2001||02:46 PM||||Greg....  Thank's I did'nt even think about that..  <BR>Oreif... I just put the cap off the totalled GT, so I'll try that. Also as far as work being done around the tank itself...  YES I pulled the tank to put in another fuel pump.  I just got under there and I don't know I'f it's right or not!!!  It all look's right. the return line is the smallest under there ..  correct??all the lines under there are a different size it look's like(sorta), there are 3 metal lines that come off the fuel pump it's self ........   Well actually 2 are one size and the other is small....  1. the return line from the canister itself!<BR>2. a bigger one goes to the fuel rail!<BR>3. this one is the same size as the one that goes to the fuel rail, this one comes from the fuel filter!<BR>Is all that right??   lolol  I'm lost I think..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> Hey guy's thank you for all your help.<BR>I love my Fiero Brother's and Sister's..<P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||01-13-2001||03:33 PM||||The Fiero gas cap is not suposed to vent. no car built after the late 70's is allowed to use vented caps. All venting is to be done thru the vapor recovery canister. ((In DE they also test the fuel tank and cap for air leaks. Some information about this testing is actually available on the Stant web site.))<P>Without a V6 to look at I can't tell you just what is flooding the vapor canister. There is definatly a problem in how the lines are hooked up. It sound like the fuel rail return line is the problem since the car is running. <P>I'm not sure exactly how these work at the tank. didn't you say you had recently replaced the pump? Are you sure the lines are installed to the correct ports on the tank? <P>Unfortunatly you did not fix this before replacing the canister so now this one is pretty much ruined as well.<P>Are you sure you have the vacuum lines hooked up right on the canister and on the block/tb? If they are wrong you could be pulling vacuum on the canister that is sucking fuel up the tank vent line. <P>It matters greatly which port on the TB the control line is connected to. If it is on the wrong TB port the control will open the purge valve at idle, which is not suposed to happen.<P>If the vac lines are reveresed you will also have problems. The vac lines are keyed by size. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 01-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Indiana_resto_guy||01-13-2001||03:40 PM||||OK, try this:<P>Since the car runs, you have the correct line hooked up for the pressure line.<BR>Swap the other two, seems to me like the vent line that goes to the canister is a short tube INSIDE the tank, to vent fumes and the other (the return line) extends into the tank somewhat.<BR>I think that the two are reversed and the vacumn source from your canister is siphoning fuel UP from the tank.<BR> If you have a full or near full tank, this seems to be a reasonable choice!<p>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 01-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||1FieroGTRacingInc||01-13-2001||04:33 PM||||Thank's Greg..  theorge.... <BR>I'll try ALL THE ABOVE IDEA'S..... <BR>I wonder WHICH LINES if hooked up WRONG, would still ALLOW  the car to start AND  run at idle forever without any problem's... OTHER then fuel pouring out the bottom of the canister?????   <P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||7
